  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 6's final failure was caused by socket-mouth alignment, not a hidden object: with the right-turn elbow at y=29..34, its rightward spill runs at y=29..31 and strikes the socket's solid top wall even though all four socket glyphs visibly change color. Moving that elbow down exactly one 3-pixel cell to y=32..37 shifts the outflow to y=32..34, through the socket's open side, removes the stray/wall contact, and wins.",
  "narrative": "Replayed the resolver's exact 278-action prefix from a fresh reset and confirmed levels_completed=5. I reconstructed the strongest prior L6 layout and instrumented its spill animation from rendered frames: it colored all four sockets but the right branch hit the solid top of the right socket at y=29..31. Moving only the right-turn elbow down one cell aligned that branch with the socket opening at y=32..34 and produced a live level-6 win. I compressed the solution to a 37-action suffix and ran reproduce() from a fresh reset; it reached level 6 with reproduced=true, completing the game's six levels in 634 total env.step() calls including exploration and the gate.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The resolver prefix is 278 actions and was directly confirmed from a fresh reset to reach levels_completed=5; any further reproduction gate needs at least those 278 calls.",
    "L6 directions are ACTION1=up, ACTION2=down, ACTION3=left, ACTION4=right; ACTION6 selects by rendered coordinate and ACTION5 commits.",
    "The vertical splitter cannot move left of x=14..16, so clearance from the left-turn elbow must be created by offsetting the elbow rather than moving the splitter toward the sockets.",
    "With the horizontal bar at x=23..37,y=20..22, place the left-turn elbow at x=20..25,y=29..34 rather than x=17..22: this changes the stream/elbow contact from the vertical stem to the horizontal arm and allows both left sockets to fill.",
    "The winning positions are: right-turn elbow x=35..40,y=32..37; left-turn elbow x=20..25,y=29..34; vertical splitter x=14..16,y=26..37; embedded-source horizontal bar x=23..37,y=20..22; then ACTION5.",
    "Coloring all four socket glyphs is not sufficient evidence of a clean route: a stream striking a socket's solid wall can color the whole glyph. Inspect whether the stream enters through the 3-pixel mouth; the right socket's mouth is y=32..34.",
    "L6 has scarce failed commits and a finite whole-level action budget, so use the 37-action one-commit suffix rather than iterating commits."
  ],
  "solve_provenance": "live_agent_self_discovery"
